\n\
Alternatively, Swampsnare Trap on Avatar Enthusiasts: {2}{B}, gives -5/-3, kills it. That's a clean single removal for 3 mana, leaving my board intact. Then I can attack with both creatures. Hog-Monkey's trigger: at beginning of combat, target creature with a +1/+1 counter gains menace — neither of my creatures has a counter, so no trigger value... Actually Hog-Monkey itself has no counters. Callous Inspector has menace naturally.\n\
\n\
Plan: Play Swamp (4th land), cast Swampsnare Trap on Avatar Enthusiasts, attack with both. Opponent at 19 takes 4 → 15.\n\
\n\
Wait — should I consider that opponent tapped out, so no combat tricks likely (they have Forest/Plains/Plains tapped — no mana for tricks). Good.\n\
\n\
