\n\
Let me sequence: first play the Swamp, then cast Swampsnare Trap. Actually order doesn't matter much, but playing land first is fine. Actually, I could cast Swampsnare Trap with 3 swamps and keep the land in hand to bluff... but playing the 4th swamp enables Day of Black Sun X=2 next turn or Treetop if I find red... no red in deck presumably. Playing the land is generally right — no reason to hold. Actually holding a land to bluff a spell could be minor value, but having 4 mana available for Day of Black Sun (X=2) on their next board commit is more valuable. Play the Swamp.\n\
\n\
Let me do: choose_action to play Swamp, then next decision cast Swampsnare Trap targeting Avatar Enthusiasts.\n\
