      "seq": 95,
      "game_seq": 236,
      "reasoning": "The opponent just played The Earth King and made a 4/4 Bear — but that Bear token has mana value 0, which means **Day of Black Sun with X=0** destroys it for just {B}{B} while leaving all my creatures (MV 1 and 3) untouched. That's a huge tempo swing. Let me chat and cast it.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the situation. I'm at 20 life, opponent at 9. Opponent has:\n\
- Bear Token 5/4 (sick — summoning sickness, can't attack but can block? No wait, \"sick\" means summoning sickness, it can't attack but CAN block... actually summoning sickness prevents attacking and tapping abilities, but blocking is fine)\n\
- Suki, Courageous Rescuer 2/4\n\
- The Earth King 3/2 (sick)\n\
- 4 lands tapped (Forest, Forest, Plains, Plains)\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- Callous Inspector 1/1 menace\n\
- Hog-Monkey 5/4 with 2 +1/+1 counters (gains menace at combat)\n\
- 5 Swamps untapped\n\
- Hand: Barrels of Blasting Jelly {1}, Callous Inspector {B}, Day of Black Sun {X}{B}{B}, Treetop Freedom Fighters {2}{R}\n\
\n\
Opponent just played The Earth King which created a 4/4 Bear token. They tapped out.\n\
\n\
Key consideration: Day of Black Sun. If I cast it with X=3, it destroys all creatures with mana value 3 or less and they lose all abilities. That would kill:\n\
- Suki (MV 3? Suki costs... let me think. Suki, Courageous Rescuer is 2/4. Its mana value — the card says \"Suki, Courageous Rescuer 2/4\" but I don't see its cost. Probably {2}{W} = MV 3.)\n\
- The Earth King (MV? The Earth King is 3/2, probably costs {3}{G} = MV 4, or maybe {2}{G} = MV 3?)\n\
- Bear Token — tokens have MV 0, so Day of Black Sun with any X kills the bear token!\n\
\n\
Wait, tokens have mana value 0. So Day of Black Sun with X=0 would destroy the Bear token (MV 0 ≤ 0). But it would also destroy... my creatures? Callous Inspector has MV 1, Hog-Monkey MV 3.\n\
\n\
Day of Black Sun: \"Each creature with mana value X or less loses all abilities until end of turn. Destroy those creatures.\" It hits ALL creatures, including mine.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
1. Cast Day of Black Sun with X=3: kills Suki (MV 3?), Earth King (MV 3-4?), Bear token (MV 0), but also kills my Callous Inspector (MV 1) and Hog-Monkey (MV 3). That clears the whole board. Costs {3}{B}{B} = 5 mana. I have exactly 5 Swamps. Hmm, but then I lose my board too. Opponent is at 9, I'm at 20. After board wipe, I have Treetop Freedom Fighters in hand ({2}{R} — but I only have Swamps! I can't cast red spells!). Wait, Treetop Freedom Fighters costs {2}{R} and I have only Swamps. I can't cast it unless I find a Mountain or Barrels of Blasting Jelly.\n\
\n\
Barrels of Blasting Jelly {1}: Add one mana of any color. So if I play Barrels (costs 1 generic), I can tap it for red to cast Treetop Freedom Fighters!\n\
\n\
So plan: Play Barrels of Blasting Jelly for {1}, then I have 4 mana left. Hmm, Treetop costs {2}{R} = 3 total. Barrels taps for red, plus 2 Swamps = cast Treetop with haste.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the attack math. Opponent at 9. My attackers: Inspector 1/1 menace, Hog-Monkey 5/4 menace (gains menace at combat from its trigger — \"At the beginning of combat on your turn, target creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it gains menace\"). Hog-Monkey has counters, so it can target itself.\n\
\n\
Blockers: Bear 5/4, Suki 2/4, Earth King 3/2. All can block (bear is sick but can block).\n\
\n\
