Hmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider: should I attack with Hog-Monkey at all? If they double-block and kill it, I lose my best creature. What if I attack with only Inspector? They take 1 (can't profitably block — double-blocking a 1/1 to kill it means taking... they'd trade 2 creatures blocking, Inspector dies, deals 1 to me, I get a Clue — actually that might be fine for them? They kill my Inspector, I draw a card. They'd rather do that than let Hog-Monkey connect... but if Hog-Monkey doesn't attack, they don't need to block at all. Take 1 → 8.)\n\
\n\
Then what? Next turn: Treetop + attack with Hog-Monkey, Inspector, Treetop, 1/1. They have Suki + EK + whatever they play. Hmm, they get another turn to deploy. They have 4 cards in hand. If they play another creature, my menace attackers get worse.\n\
\n\
I think attacking with both now is right — pressure them at 9 life. If they trade Suki for Hog-Monkey, that's acceptable; they fall to 8 with my board of Inspector + (postcombat) Barrels, and next turn Treetop.\n\
\n\
Actually, one more thought — the damage ordering if they double block Hog-Monkey with Suki + EK: I choose to kill Suki (the engine). Assign 4 to Suki, 1 to EK. Yes.\n\
\n\
Alternatively assign 2 to EK (EK has 2 toughness... wait, does EK get +1/+0 — power only, toughness stays 2). Kill EK with 2, 3 to Suki — Suki survives (4 toughness). Then board: them Suki 2/4. Suki alone is weak offensively. Hmm, which kill is better? Suki: anthem + token maker, 2/4 body. EK: 3/2, ramps when power-4+ creatures attack — but they have no power-4 creatures left if Bear is dead... unless Suki anthems... no, Suki gives +1/+0, EK becomes 4/2 — power 4! So EK attacking with Suki out = EK has power 4 → ramp trigger. Together they're synergistic. Killing either breaks it. Suki is the stronger card (token engine + anthem). Kill Suki.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, actually, also consider: they might block with just... no, menace prevents single blocks.\n\
\n\
Decision: attack with both Inspector and Hog-Monkey.\n\
\n\
Also, Hog-Monkey's begin-combat trigger: \"target creature you control with a +1/+1 counter gains menace\" — only Hog-Monkey has counters; it already has menace. Target it anyway (or maybe the trigger can target... only creatures with counters — only Hog-Monkey). Fine, redundant.\n\
\n\
Let me attack with both. Then handle the trigger, then postcombat play Barrels.\n\
\n\
Rationale: Swing with both menace creatures; opponent can only block one of them. Worst case they trade Suki for Hog-Monkey and stilltake damage.",
