\n\
Opponent: 7hp, Bear Token 4/4 (sick), The Earth King 2/2, all lands tapped, 4 cards in hand.\n\
\n\
I have 2 untapped Swamps. Beetle-Headed Merchants costs {4}{B} = 5 mana. I can't cast it this turn with only 2 untapped. \n\
\n\
Treetop Freedom Fighters costs {2}{R} = 3 mana. I only have 2 untapped Swamps, and Barrels already used its once-per-turn mana ability this turn (I activated it earlier this turn). So I can't cast Freedom Fighters this turn.\n\
\n\
Wait, the clue draw — I cracked the Clue and drew... looking at my hand: Beetle-Headed Merchants, Swamp, Treetop Freedom Fighters. So I drew a Swamp from the Clue (hand previously was Beetle-Headed Merchants, Treetop Freedom Fighters after casting the second Inspector... actually let me not worry).\n\
\n\
So the only play available is playing the Swamp land. That gives me 6 Swamps total (one tapped... wait, 4 tapped + 2 untapped + new one = 7 lands? Let me count: bf shows Swamp (tapped) x4, Swamp, Swamp = 6 Swamps, plus Barrels. Playing this Swamp makes 7 lands.\n\
\n\
With 7 lands next turn, I can cast Beetle-Headed Merchants (5 mana) and still have 2 left over. Or cast Freedom Fighters with red from Barrels.\n\
\n\
Should I play the Swamp? Yes, definitely — playing a land is free and enables Merchants next turn. No reason to hold it... well, holding could bluff, but the land drop is more valuable. Play the Swamp.\n\
\n\
Then pass. Next turn: 7 lands untap. I can cast Beetle-Headed Merchants for 5, leaving 2. Opponent at 7 life with a 4/4 Bear (no longer sick next turn — it will be able to block) and Earth King 2/2.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about next turn's attack. Opponent's Bear will be unsick on their turn 8, and they can attack with it plus Earth King toramp lands. But that's their turn.\n\
\n\
For now: play Swamp, pass the turn.",
