\n\
My plan: next turn I can attack with Merchants and sacrifice Inspector to draw a card and grow Merchants. Opponent is at 7.\n\
\n\
If I block the Bear with Merchants, both die. Then I have Inspector, Mountain, 6 Swamps, Barrels. My hand: Treetop Freedom Fighters. I could cast Freedom Fighters (2/1 haste) with Mountain red. But opponent has lots of blockers.\n\
\n\
If I block with Inspector: Inspector dies, I take 1 (to 12 effectively, but I don't take the 4 combat damage). Wait — Inspector blocks Bear: Bear deals 4 to Inspector (lethal), Inspector deals 1 to Bear. Inspector dies, triggers: deals 1 damage to me, create Clue. So I go from 13 to 12. Bear survives as 4/4 (took 1, has 4 toughness, so it's now damaged but heals at end of turn... actually damage wears off at cleanup, so Bear is fine next turn).\n\
\n\
If I don't block: I take 4, go to 9.\n\
\n\
Hmm. Blocking with Inspector saves 3 life net (4 damage prevented, 1 self-damage) but loses Inspector and gives me a Clue.\n\
\n\
Blocking with Merchants trades my best creature for their token. Bad.\n\
\n\
Not blocking: I go to 9, keep both creatures.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — what's my clock? Opponent at 7. Next turn (turn 9), I can attack with Merchants (5/4) and Inspector (1/1 menace). Merchants trigger: sacrifice Inspector, draw a card, Merchants becomes 6/5. Then opponent needs to block Merchants 6/5. They have Earth King 2/2, Toph 2/3, Suki 5/4, Bear 4/4, Forest 2/2. They can block with Bear + something to kill it.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually, let me think about lethal. Opponent at 7. If I attack with Merchants and Inspector (sacced to trigger), Merchants 6/5. They block with Bear 4/4 + Toph 2/3 maybe: 6 damage assigned... Merchants kills both (4+2=6 toughness), takes 6 damage, dies (5 toughness). Trade. Then I draw a card.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, attack with Merchants alone, keep Inspector for later sacrifice.\n\
\n\
What's the opponent's threat? Suki Kyoshi Warrior attacks next turn, creates an Ally token, power = number of creatures. They have 5 creatures now; if Bear attacks... wait, the Bear is attacking now. After combat, they still have 5 creatures (unless I kill one).\n\
\n\
Their board next turn: Suki 5/4 can attack (makes a token, becomes 6 power), Bear 4/4, Forest 2/2, Earth King 2/2, Toph 2/3. If they swing with everything: 5+4+2+2+2 = 15 damage plus token 1 = 16. I'd need to block. Merchants can block one. Inspector can block one (menace only matters on attack).\n\
\n\
Actually I'm at 13 now. If I take 4 from Bear, I'm at 9. Next turn they could attack with Suki (5/4 + token), Bear 4/4, Forest 2/2, Earth King 2/2, Toph 2/3. Total power: 5+4+2+2+2=15 + 1 token = 16 damage. I block with Merchants (kills one, maybe trades) and Inspector. I'd take a lot.\n\
\n\
But I have a turn 9 attack first. Let me think about whether I can win the race.\n\
\n\
Actually, maybe I should just block the Bear with Inspector. I go to 12 (taking 1 from the trigger), get a Clue. Then turn 9: attack with Merchants, sacrifice... hmm, if Inspector is dead, I sacrifice the Clue token instead! Merchants' trigger says \"sacrifice another creature or artifact\" — Clue is an artifact. So I can attack with Merchants, sacrifice the Clue to draw a card and grow Merchants to 6/5. \n\
\n\
That works nicely. Block with Inspector, get Clue, then next turn Merchants attacks, sac Clue, draw, Merchants 6/5.\n\
\n\
Opponent blocks Merchants 6/5 with Bear 4/4 + Earth King 2/2: Merchants kills both, takes 6, dies. Or they block with just Bear: Bear dies, Merchants takes 4, survives as 6/5 with 4 damage... wait 5 toughness, 4 damage, survives with 1 toughness left. Then opponent at 7 takes... no, blocked, no trample. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Actually, what's my path to winning? Opponent at 7. I need to deal 7 damage. \n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Treetop Freedom Fighters: 2/1 haste, makes a 1/1 Ally. That's 3 power of haste. But they have blockers.\n\
- Barrels of Blasting Jelly: {5}, {T}, sac: deal 5 damage to target creature. That can kill Suki or Bear.\n\
\n\
