      "thinking": "Let me think about the current state. I attacked with Beetle-Headed Merchants (5/4). Its attack trigger is on the stack: \"you may sacrifice another creature or artifact. If you do, draw a card and put a +1/+1 counter on it.\"\n\
\n\
I have a Clue Token on the battlefield. I want to sacrifice the Clue Token to the Merchants' trigger to draw a card and grow Merchants to 6/5.\n\
\n\
The choices shown: Clue Token [id=p92, activate] — that's the Clue's own sacrifice ability ({2}, sac: draw a card). But the Merchants trigger is on the stack and I need to choose whether to sacrifice something.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually the current decision is \"Play instants and activated abilities\" — the trigger is on the stack. The choice to sacrifice for the trigger may come when the trigger resolves. Right now I can activate the Clue Token's ability (crack it for {2}) or pass.\n\
\n\
I have 2 untapped lands. If I crack the Clue now, I draw a card before deciding on the Merchants trigger sacrifice. But wait — if I crack the Clue now, I won't have it to sacrifice to the Merchants trigger. The Merchants trigger needs \"another creature or artifact\" to sacrifice. My other artifacts/creatures: just the Clue Token (Merchants itself can't be sacrificed to its own trigger — \"another\"). So if I crack the Clue now, I have nothing to sacrifice for the Merchants trigger.\n\
\n\
So I should NOT crack the Clue. I should pass priority and let the Merchants trigger resolve, choosing to sacrifice the Clue Token to draw a card and put a +1/+1 counter on Merchants.\n\
\n\
Wait, but the prompt said \"Attacking with Beetle-Headed Merchants — I'll sacrifice the Clue token to its trigger to draw a card and grow it to 6/5\". So yes, the plan is to sacrifice the Clue to the trigger.\n\
\n\
So now I pass priority so the trigger resolves. When it resolves, I'll be prompted to choose what to sacrifice (or maybe \"you may\" — choose yes, then pick the Clue).\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider: could I crack the Clue now AND still have a sacrifice target? My artifacts/creatures other than Merchants: Clue Token only. Lands aren't creatures (Mountain, Swamps). So no. If I crack the Clue, the trigger does nothing (I could still choose not to sacrifice). Drawing a card now vs. drawing a card from the trigger — same card draw, but the trigger also gives a +1/+1 counter. So sacrificing the Clue to the trigger is strictly better: draw a card AND grow Merchants to6/5.\n\
\n\
So pass priority now.",
